# ####################################################################################
# VENDOR RESTOCK
# ####################################################################################
# Moves sellable items from a source container onto the vendor, one stack per item
# type, prints the price you should charge, and waits while you type it.
#
# PREREQUISITE
#   Vendor Settings, Use Item Pricing Menu must be ON so gump 685310710 opens.
#   Gump id 685310710, the same one the vendor pricing menu opens.
#
# WHY THE PRICE IS TYPED BY HAND
#   Razor scripts cannot type into a gump text field. gumpresponse sends a button id
#   only. So the script does everything except the typing, and tells you the number.
#
# HOW IT RUNS
#   Phase 1 collects every sellable stack from the source container into a list, one
#   while loop per item family so the graphic lists stay readable.
#   Phase 2 walks that list. For each stack it reads the label, picks the price, lifts
#   the whole stack, drops it on the vendor, waits for gump 685310710, prints
#   item name : price , then waits until the gump is really gone.
#   Clicking the small orb refreshes the gump, so the script confirms it stays closed
#   for var__delay_gump_settle before moving on. Toggle war mode to abort.
#
# PRICES
#   This file is the source of truth, not library/vendor-prices.md.
#   Each PRICE block lists the variable, the searchable item name and the item id, so
#   you can paste the name into the Outlands Portal vendor search, and still identify
#   a price you later stop using.
#   0 means the price is not set yet.
#   It has to be a number. Razor coerces an interpolated variable to an integer, so a
#   text placeholder like --- comes out as 4294967295, which is -1 unsigned.
#
# LABEL CASE
#   The in operator is case sensitive. Confirmed in game that item labels are
#   lowercase, for example  chromatic distillation , so the lowercase match strings
#   in the PICK PRICE block are correct.
#
# DROP LAYOUT
#   Razor has no arithmetic, so a fixed cell is baked into every item type at edit time.
#   The vendor container is round, so the cells follow an ellipse centred on 190 205 with
#   radii 148 and 168, 15 pixels apart. Each section starts on a fresh row, so a section
#   reads as one contiguous band. An item type always lands in the same cell, so the
#   arrangement is identical every run.
#   Rows used 21 of 22. If items land outside the barrel, shrink the radii here.
#
# NOT INCLUDED
#   Currency graphics 2539 3821 3891 5360 16898 from script/loot/distribution.razor
#   are left out on purpose. Gold, doubloons, prevalia coins and checks are not stock.

clearsysmsg
clearall
clearignore
cleardragdrop

# ####################################################################################
# CONFIG - CONTAINERS
# ####################################################################################
#   var__vendor_container   the vendor you are stocking
#   var__source_container   the box your sellable items are sitting in
# Both are opened with dclick first so the client knows their contents.
# Each is asked for once and kept in your Razor profile, so no serial sits in this
# shared file. To point the script at something else, run  unsetvar var__vendor_container
# from another script and rerun this one.
# ####################################################################################
if not varexist var__vendor_container
    overhead "Target the vendor you are stocking" 55
    setvar var__vendor_container
endif

if not varexist var__source_container
    overhead "Target the box holding what you want to sell" 55
    setvar var__source_container
endif

# ####################################################################################
# CONFIG - BEHAVIOUR
# ####################################################################################
#   var__auto_place         0 stops on each gump so you can type the price
#                           1 presses Place Item for Sale, everything lands at 99,999
#   var__lift_amount        60000 is the UO stack cap, so this takes a whole stack
#   var__delay_gump_settle  raise it if the script jumps ahead while you are typing
# ####################################################################################
@setvar! var__auto_place 0
@setvar! var__lift_amount 60000
@setvar! var__delay_open 700
@setvar! var__delay_lift 600
@setvar! var__delay_place 800
@setvar! var__delay_poll 200
@setvar! var__delay_gump_settle 1200
# How often the item name and price is repeated over your head while you type.
@setvar! var__delay_hint_repeat 2000

